<title>USA: GE's Medical Systems unit names Immelt CEO.</title>
<headline>GE's Medical Systems unit names Immelt CEO.</headline>
<dateline>FAIRFIELD, CONN. 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Electric Co's Medical Systems unit said it named Jeffrey Immelt its president and chief executive, effectively immediately, to replace John Trani, who resigned to become chairman and CEO of the Stanley Works.</p>
<p>Immelt, 40, had formerly been vice president of the Americas at GE's Plastics unit.</p>
<p>He joined GE in 1982. He will be based in Milwaukee, where GE Medical Systems is located, the company said.</p>
<p>GE Medical Systems makes medical diognostic imaging products.</p>
